Original commit body from 5eae01425d767db5fabc09ae5a47b0e871413f6f:

Caught on the dev push pipeline for 6e92792a34 — the WI-fodad merge itself —
which printed

    fatal: bad object 66737979dee9a56daeebf55731181ddf057ac53c
    ✅ PR changes no .py files — skipping pytest

and reported SUCCESS having run zero tests, on a commit changing nine files
including four Python ones.

Two defects compounding.

(1) A FAILED git diff IS BYTE-IDENTICAL TO A CLEAN ONE. The condition was
    [ -z "$(git diff --name-only "$BASE" "$HEAD" | grep -E '\.py$' || true)" ].
    A diff that errors writes nothing to stdout, so the gate could not tell
    "nothing changed" from "I could not find out", and resolved that ambiguity
    by skipping the suite. Now the diff and its exit status are captured
    separately and the skip fires only on a SUCCESSFUL diff that genuinely
    reported no .py files. Same block WI-modur repaired, different hole: that
    fix changed which question the gate asks, this changes what it does when it
    cannot get an answer (L54, default-deny).

(2) THE BASE WAS A REWRITTEN COMMIT, SYSTEMATICALLY. CI_PREV_COMMIT_SHA is the
    previous PIPELINE's commit, not the previous tip of this branch. auto-pr
    merges by rebase, which rewrites the commit, so after every rebase merge
    that SHA names an object absent from the clone. Verified: 66737979de is the
    pre-rebase copy of 6e92792a34, reachable only from the feature branch
    auto-pr had just deleted, and NOT an ancestor of dev. This fired on every
    rebase-merged push, not intermittently. The base is now validated with
    git cat-file -e before use, falling back to HEAD^ only when it does not
    resolve — scoped deliberately, since always diffing HEAD^ would undercount
    a push landing more than one commit.

Mutation-tested both ways against the extracted shell block (which is executed,
not read): reinstating either the one-line diff or the unvalidated base turns
exactly the corresponding new test red.

Fifth distinct route in the L48 family and the second inside this one block.

